-- title:
--   Chart endomorphism fixing the reduction agrees with the inclusion mod I
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ and $B_1$ be commutative rings with $B_1$ a $B$-algebra whose structure map $B \to B_1$ is surjective, and write $I = \ker(B \to B_1)$. Let $X$, $X_1$ be schemes, $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} B$, $f_1 : X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ and $g : X_1 \to X$ morphisms such that the square with sides $g$, $f_1$, $f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $B \to B_1$ is a pullback (so $X_1$ is the base change of $X$ along $\operatorname{Spec} B_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B$). Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ that is affine, and let $\alpha : U \to U$ be a morphism of schemes such that the restriction $g \mid_U : g^{-1}(U) \to U$ followed by $\alpha$ equals $g \mid_U$. Equip $C = \Gamma(X, U)$ with the $B$-algebra structure coming from $f$, namely the ring map $B \to C$ obtained from the inverse of the global-sections isomorphism for $\operatorname{Spec} B$ followed by $f$ on sections over $\top$ and $U$. Let $J = I \cdot C$ be the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of $I$. Then $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $C \to C/J$, followed by the canonical map $\operatorname{Spec} C \to X$ attached to the affine open $U$, equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $C \to C/J$ followed by the inverse of the isomorphism $U \cong \operatorname{Spec} C$, then $\alpha$, then the open immersion $U \hookrightarrow X$.
--
--   This says that an endomorphism $\alpha$ of an affine chart $U$ which fixes the reduction $g \mid_U$ induces the identity on the chart modulo $I$: the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}(C/IC) \to X$ obtained from $\alpha$ and from the inclusion of $U$ coincide. It is the direction complementary to the passage from a congruence modulo $IC$ to a chart endomorphism, and is used in the analysis of bare deformations of a scheme with good reduction, where chart endomorphisms and overlap isomorphisms have to be compared on slices.
